📉 3. KL Divergence

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 What is KL Divergence?

KL Divergence measures:

```text id="r3x9qp"
Difference between two probability distributions
```

---

📌 Simple Meaning

👉 How different is **new model vs old model**

---

📊 Formula

```text id="z7k2mp"
KL(P || Q) = Σ P(x) log(P(x) / Q(x))
```

---

🔹 Intuition

* Small KL → models are similar
* Large KL → models are very different

---

🎯 Why KL Divergence is Used?

✔ Controls model updates
✔ Prevents drastic changes
✔ Maintains stability

---

🔗 PPO + KL Divergence Connection

👉 In RLHF:

* PPO updates model
* KL Divergence ensures updates are **not too large**

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📊 Example (Concept)

Old model:

```text id="y6k1qp"
"AI is good"
```

New model:

```text id="c8x3mz"
"AI is extremely powerful and transformative"
```

👉 KL Divergence measures how different outputs are.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚔️ PPO vs Traditional RL

| Feature   | Traditional RL | PPO          |
| --------- | -------------- | ------------ |
| Stability | Low            | High         |
| Updates   | Large          | Controlled   |
| Usage     | General RL     | LLM training |

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Why This Matters for LLMs

✔ Improves response quality
✔ Aligns model with human values
✔ Prevents harmful outputs
✔ Enables safe AI systems

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📚 Key Takeaways

✔ PPO is used to fine-tune models using RL
✔ It ensures stable and controlled learning
✔ KL Divergence measures difference between models
✔ PPO + KL is core in RLHF (used in ChatGPT)

